            "body": "Thanks for taking this on. I compared the PR with the current vLLM contributing guidelines and found a few items to address before review:\r\n\r\n1. **PR title classification**: The guidelines say PR titles must use one or more of the documented prefixes (`[Bugfix]`, `[CI/Build]`, `[Doc]`, `[Misc]`, etc.). `fix(deps): ...` is not one of the listed prefixes. Please retitle this using the appropriate documented category, likely `[CI/Build]` or `[Misc]` depending on how the maintainers classify dependency/image maintenance.\r\n\r\n2. **Lint/CI validation is not currently green**: `pre-run-check` failed because the PR has none of the `verified`, `ready`, or `ready-run-all-tests` labels and the author has 0 merged PRs; consequently the `pre-commit` job was skipped. The contributing guidelines require all linter checks to pass. Please ask a maintainer to apply the appropriate label and rerun the workflow so the pre-commit result is recorded. The required `buildkite/ci/pr` check is also still pending.\r\n\r\n3. **Test and validation evidence is missing**: The guidelines require sufficient tests, and the PR description claims compatibility with `torch==2.13.0` and the Phi-3-Vision processor without showing test commands or results. Please add targeted validation or link to CI evidence covering dependency installation/import, the Phi-3-Vision processor, and the rebuilt image containing `torchvision==0.28.1`; please also confirm that the relevant container scanner finding is cleared.\r\n\r\nWhat is already in good shape: the PR targets `main`, links issue #51192, keeps the change limited to the relevant requirements file, and passes DCO (`Signed-off-by` is present). Being an external contributor is not itself a problem; the contributing documentation welcomes contributions from everyone.\r\n\r\nReference: https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing/",
